DFT calculations to support surface binding energies were performed to further verify the rationality of the optimal growth orientation of $\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{O}_{4}$ , as shown in Figure 4. The initial stage for the crystal growth requires atomic nucleation on the substrate, followed by the orientated growth along the most stable facet. The energy values shown for different facets represent the energy to be released when the next periodic cell binds to the current given facet per unit area. The extension along the (111) facet of $\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{O}_{4}$ after nucleation was found as optimum thermodynamically directed orientation because of the exergonic process with $-0.197\mathrm{eV}/\mathrm{\AA}^{2}.$ .
